Ground truth for the codemap agent benchmark — INDEPENDENCE RULE
================================================================

Every *.json file in this directory is the frozen, correct answer for one task,
derived at the pinned fixture SHA (bench/fixtures/fixture.lock).

Ground truth is produced INDEPENDENTLY OF CODEMAP — never by a codemap
invocation, and never from codemap's graph package. If any truth file were
regenerated from codemap, the "with codemap" arm would win by construction and
the benchmark would be worthless. The oracle here is the Go type checker itself:

  bench/tasks/truth/gen/  is a standalone program that loads the fixture with
  go/types (via golang.org/x/tools/go/packages — the same independent type
  information gopls exposes) and computes callers, callees, definitions,
  blast radius (inbound BFS), covering tests (transitive inbound to Test funcs),
  call-path edges, file outlines, and rename-impact counts directly from type
  info. It imports nothing from codemap.

Which symbol each task points at is recorded, auditable, in targets.json.

Regenerate (only when fixture.lock's SHA changes, or targets.json changes):

  bench/fixtures/fetch.sh                 # ensure the pinned fixture is present
  go run ./bench/tasks/truth/gen          # rewrites the *.json here

A SHA bump means re-deriving AND re-reviewing all truth — treat it as a
deliberate, reviewed change. For the transitive tasks (04 blast_radius,
05 covering_tests, 07 call_path) a human should skim the regenerated sets and
confirm they look right before committing; the derivation is auditable per task
from targets.json + the fixture source.
